Can't get away with that without a terminator.

I will admit that {cu} in every bridi is more a personal pet-peeve
than anything else. I find it distasteful/lazy. My real point is that
all terminators should be taught along with their corresponding tag/
gadri. The only way to really reinforce memorisation is through use.

I'll have to ask, but I wonder if it aids in reading comprehension. Do
students that learn to use {cu} early on rely upon {cu} to identify
the selbri? Do students that don't learn {cu} learn to identify the
selbri more easily?

We should set up a research experiment.

